<https://w3id.org/lmodel/slsa/SlsaResult> OIO:inSubset <https://w3id.org/lmodel/slsa/slsa_build_track> , <https://w3id.org/lmodel/slsa/slsa_source_track> ;
	rdfs:seeAlso "https://slsa.dev/spec/v1.2/verification_summary#slsaresult"^^xsd:anyURI , "https://slsa.dev/spec/v1.2/verified-properties"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:inScheme "https://w3id.org/lmodel/slsa/slsa_verification"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:note "Issuers may add values of their own, but none that start with SLSA_; this enum lists the SLSA-defined values, and slsa_result_value, which verified_levels takes, admits both." , "Only FAILED has a public term: it means EARL's failed, as SlsaVerificationResult's FAILED does, since a VSA lists it only when verification failed. No vocabulary names SLSA's levels or verified properties." , "The working-draft Dependency and Build Environment tracks name no results yet, so none are listed for them." ;
	linkml:definition_uri "https://w3id.org/lmodel/slsa/SlsaResult"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	linkml:description "A result of evaluating an artifact against SLSA: a track level, a verified property, or a failure. A level implies the levels below it in the same track." ;
	linkml:permissible_values <https://w3id.org/lmodel/slsa/FAILED> , <https://w3id.org/lmodel/slsa/SLSA_BUILD_LEVEL_0> , <https://w3id.org/lmodel/slsa/SLSA_BUILD_LEVEL_1> , <https://w3id.org/lmodel/slsa/SLSA_BUILD_LEVEL_2> , <https://w3id.org/lmodel/slsa/SLSA_BUILD_LEVEL_3> , <https://w3id.org/lmodel/slsa/SLSA_BUILD_LEVEL_UNEVALUATED> , <https://w3id.org/lmodel/slsa/SLSA_BUILD_REPRODUCED> , <https://w3id.org/lmodel/slsa/SLSA_SOURCE_LEVEL_0> , <https://w3id.org/lmodel/slsa/SLSA_SOURCE_LEVEL_1> , <https://w3id.org/lmodel/slsa/SLSA_SOURCE_LEVEL_2> , <https://w3id.org/lmodel/slsa/SLSA_SOURCE_LEVEL_3> , <https://w3id.org/lmodel/slsa/SLSA_SOURCE_LEVEL_4> , <https://w3id.org/lmodel/slsa/SLSA_SOURCE_LEVEL_UNEVALUATED> , <https://w3id.org/lmodel/slsa/SLSA_SOURCE_TWO_PARTY_REVIEWED> .
